# Apptainer definition file for Transition.
#
# This builds on top of the Docker image already produced by the project's
# own CI (see .github/workflows/build-docker-image.yml), instead of
# duplicating the Dockerfile. Rebuild whenever a specific Transition version
# should be pinned, by changing the tag below.
#
# Build (on a machine where you have root, or via a remote/CI builder --
# Calcul Quebec login/compute nodes do not allow this):
#   apptainer build transition.sif transition.def
#
# See ../docs/runOnHPC.md for full usage instructions, including how to run
# PostGIS and how to launch a batch calculation job under SLURM.

Bootstrap: docker
From: chairemobilite/transition:latest

%labels
    Maintainer Chaire Mobilite en transport
    Application Transition

%help
    Apptainer image for running Transition (including batch routing and
    batch accessibility map calculations) on HPC clusters such as those
    managed by Calcul Quebec / the Digital Research Alliance of Canada.

    This image only contains the application itself. It expects:
      - A reachable PostGIS database (see docs/runOnHPC.md to run one as a
        separate Apptainer instance).
      - A project directory bind-mounted (config.js, .env, and a
        pre-populated runtime/ directory with any OSM/OSRM data prepared
        ahead of time, since compute nodes usually have no internet access).

    Examples:
      apptainer exec --bind /path/to/project:/config transition.sif \
          sh -c "yarn migrate"

      apptainer exec --bind /path/to/project:/config transition.sif \
          yarn node packages/transition-backend/lib/scripts/listTasks.task.js

%environment
    export PROJECT_CONFIG=${PROJECT_CONFIG:-/config/config.js}
    export TRANSITION_DOTENV=${TRANSITION_DOTENV:-/config/.env}

%runscript
    exec "$@"
